# Cursor Rules for FileSynchronizer (.NET 9 / C# 13 / WPF)

- Target .NET 9 (`net9.0-windows`), C# 13.
- Use file-scoped namespaces (`namespace FileSynchronizer...;`).
- Nullable reference types are strictly enforced; avoid `!` when possible.
- Core library (`FileSynchronizer.Core`) must remain platform/UI agnostic (no WPF references).
- Use `System.IO.Hashing.XxHash64` for file checksums.
- Always implement two-phase synchronization: Diff/Plan first, then Execute.
- All file write operations must be atomic (write to temp file, atomic overwrite) and preserve file metadata timestamps.
- MVVM pattern in `FileSynchronizer.UI`: use `ObservableObject`, `RelayCommand`, and dispatch UI-bound changes with `Application.Current.Dispatcher`.
- When writing tests, use xUnit and test in isolated temporary directories.
